	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"Learn rotation, stress, belts, funnels, basins, deployers and contraptions in the two main Create chapters before treating every addon block as a shortcut."
				"Search JEI by mod name and Ponder every component that offers a scene. Check both the recipe and the uses of an unfamiliar machine so you understand what enters, what leaves and what powers it."
				"Build addon experiments on a small test shaft. Connecting an unknown block directly to the town factory is how one confusing machine becomes six confusing machines."
				"Create addons extend the same readable machine language into kitchens, railways, decoration, and experience processing. Ponder addon blocks when available and use JEI when their recipe type is unfamiliar."
			]
			id: "3CBF571C33BA4578"
			rewards: [{
				id: "44EDCDE10FC351AC"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Addons extend Create; they do not replace its basic grammar"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0E663135DD26D8D8"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Read the Create Addon Map"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3CBF571C33BA4578"]
			description: [
				"Central Kitchen provides Create-compatible methods for food processing and storage integrations, especially around Farmer's Delight. It is the bridge between a working kitchen and a visible food factory."
				"Choose one meal with a repeatable ingredient chain. Automate washing, cutting, mixing or packing only where JEI shows an integration recipe; ordinary Cooking Pot recipes may still need the correct containers."
				"Keep a manual kitchen beside the line. Automation should supply the community, not make it impossible to cook when a belt jams."
				"Central Kitchen and Slice and Dice automate Farmer's Delight by moving ingredients through familiar Create logistics. Stabilise the manual recipe first so the machine has a known correct result to reproduce."
			]
			id: "0D4B75EF5618911F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "372E60A287419E8A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Move prepared food through a real production line"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2F1D773CED8DB3EB"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Create: Central Kitchen"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3CBF571C33BA4578"]
			description: [
				"Slice and Dice focuses on Create automation for Farmer's Delight processes. Its machines reproduce preparation steps that normally use knives, cutting boards and kitchen handling."
				"Ponder its components, then verify the exact recipe in JEI. Pay attention to held tools, basin positions and output sides; a correct ingredient in the wrong process is still the wrong recipe."
				"Start with a high-volume staple such as vegetables or dough. A tiny line that reliably feeds everyone is a better lesson than an unfinished wall of every food in JEI."
				"Central Kitchen and Slice and Dice automate Farmer's Delight by moving ingredients through familiar Create logistics. Stabilise the manual recipe first so the machine has a known correct result to reproduce."
			]
			id: "7F45F36FB147AD0A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B51CEA3AF7207D0"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Automate the cutting board without forgetting the tool"
			tasks: [{
				id: "649752EB46E902E9"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Slice and Dice"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3CBF571C33BA4578"]
			description: [
				"Create: Enchantment Industry adds liquid experience, tanks and machines for moving enchantment work into a factory. The Disenchanter removes enchantments and captures experience instead of discarding the whole opportunity."
				"Treat enchanted loot as a decision: keep the item, salvage the enchantment path or convert unwanted work into stored experience. Never feed named or borrowed gear into a line without checking it."
				"Build an Experience Hatch near the tank so players can deliberately deposit or withdraw levels. Label input chests so ordinary repair gear cannot enter the system by accident."
				"Enchantment Industry treats experience as a resource that can be collected, moved, and applied. Label fluid routes carefully and never test an unproven process on the team's only high-level enchanted tool."
			]
			id: "5A53AAEC0E3B4B96"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4F404B3AC8369ADE"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Turn loose levels into a stored resource"
			tasks: [{
				id: "60ECED289908D9A0"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Enchantment Industry: Liquid Experience"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5A53AAEC0E3B4B96"]
			description: [
				"The Printer can copy written books, enchanted books, name tags and train schedules when supplied with the correct material or fluid. Blaze-powered stations handle enchanting and anvil-like combining."
				"Use JEI and Ponder for the installed version before spending rare books. Hyper-enchanting is an advanced extension with extra experience costs and configured limits, not the beginner starting point."
				"The first useful project is often copying a public instruction book or train schedule. Power is safer when the factory's first product is documentation."
				"Enchantment Industry treats experience as a resource that can be collected, moved, and applied. Label fluid routes carefully and never test an unproven process on the team's only high-level enchanted tool."
			]
			id: "40F22C4CB919465D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6E585EB3E60E603B"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Automate knowledge after you understand the original"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3E88EB1D5CABD989"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Printers, Enchanters and Forgers"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0D4B75EF5618911F", "40F22C4CB919465D"]
			description: [
				"Steam 'n' Rails adds custom track materials and railway components while keeping Create's station and schedule foundation. Different gauges and decorative track are choices for a coherent network, not random loot."
				"Select a standard for public routes before laying kilometres of rail. Test curves, slopes, portals and platform clearances with the actual carriage you plan to use."
				"Use semaphores and signs to show what the signals are doing. A beautiful railway is only useful when a new driver can tell which line is safe."
				"Steam 'n' Rails expands track and train options, but every junction increases operational complexity. Add signs, signals, and maintenance access before a second route turns the first into a collision puzzle."
			]
			id: "41BE0FF67B399896"
			rewards: [{
				id: "634CC21505D6BA3A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Track types, semaphores and conductors expand the railway language"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7D88EA87A21F7FB9"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Steam 'n' Rails: More Than Decoration"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["41BE0FF67B399896"]
			description: [
				"Assemble trains on straight track at a station, name stations clearly and use schedules to describe destinations and conditions. Duplicate station names create ambiguous routing."
				"Signals divide track into protected sections. Test a single passing loop with two trains before scaling up, and keep junctions visible enough to diagnose."
				"Write the passenger route on signs and in a copied schedule book. Timetables do not need to be realistic; they need to be understandable."
				"Steam 'n' Rails expands track and train options, but every junction increases operational complexity. Add signs, signals, and maintenance access before a second route turns the first into a collision puzzle."
			]
			id: "00BF4EDDD146CDD9"
			rewards: [{
				id: "0764D7B23EC4BAE8"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "A train becomes infrastructure when it can run predictably"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3A1DEF119AD428AC"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Stations, Signals and Schedules"
			x: 6.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["40F22C4CB919465D"]
			description: [
				"Copycat blocks mimic another block's appearance while keeping useful shapes. Create: Connected, Create Deco, Rechiseled Create and framed blocks add factory details, windows, panels and structural options."
				"Use these to hide awkward gaps and repeat a palette, not to conceal every moving part. Leave inspection windows around belts, shafts and filters that players may need to repair."
				"A Create workshop should look like it belongs in Minecraft and explain itself at a glance: power zone, processing zone, storage zone and safe walkway."
				"Copycats, Connected, Deco, and Rechiseled Create help machinery belong in a build. Leave the functional blocks identifiable; camouflage should improve the workshop, not conceal the part that needs repair."
			]
			id: "560A026C808FC416"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7FB8EE516C1B6759"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Let machines inherit the language of the building"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4C1F46F5520C7799"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Copycats, Connected and Deco"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["00BF4EDDD146CDD9", "560A026C808FC416"]
			description: [
				"Stop belts and deployers when their output storage is full. Avoid loose item piles, permanently stalled contraptions and dozens of tiny farms all solving the same resource."
				"Prefer batch processing and shared production. Observe server performance after adding a large line, especially if it moves mobs, fluids or many block entities."
				"Mechanical beauty includes an off switch. Label it, test it and teach another player how to use it before calling the factory finished."
				"Enchantment Industry treats experience as a resource that can be collected, moved, and applied. Label fluid routes carefully and never test an unproven process on the team's only high-level enchanted tool."
			]
			id: "4D4F9D8F293B3637"
			rewards: [{
